neutron: backport stock IRQ-completion + fixes from nxp-imx lf-6.12.y

NavQ's kernel (NXP-Robotics/linux-imx, imx95-navq-lf-6.12.y) carries an older
drivers/staging/neutron than stock nxp-imx/linux-imx lf-6.12.y. The fork hardwires
inference completion to polling mode (inf->poll_mode = true) and never arms the
inference-done IRQ, so on i.MX95 the NPU boots and clocks up but every invoke ends
in "Inference poll timeout" (Neutron Driver code=1497) and the imx-neutron-mailbox
IRQ (GIC_SPI 318 / Linux GICv3 350) count stays at 0. The Verdin i.MX95, which runs
the stock driver, completes because it waits on the inference-done IRQ.

Backport the stock driver delta (self-contained to drivers/staging/neutron; Kconfig,
Makefile, uapi and the other headers are byte-identical between fork and stock):
 - neutron_driver.c:   add 'use_irq' module param (default true) -> NEUTRON_USE_IRQ_MODE,
                       re-enable IRQ on resume
 - neutron_device.{c,h}: add neutron_irq_enable() + the IRQ-enable bit defines + flag
 - neutron_inference.c: use IRQ mode when the flag is set; pm_runtime_get/put_sync and
                       a mutex around send_reset; kref guard on the done path
 - neutron_mailbox.c:  clear APPSTATUS via W1C in the IRQ handler

Upstream-Status: Backport [nxp-imx/linux-imx lf-6.12.y; should be merged into NXP-Robotics/linux-imx]
Signed-off-by: Leonardo Bornia <leonardo.bornia@toradex.com>

--- a/drivers/staging/neutron/neutron_driver.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/neutron/neutron_driver.c
@@ -40,6 +40,11 @@
 module_param(power_mode, int, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(power_mode, "Power consumption strategy mode, 0:auto balance mode; 1:best performance mode; 2:low power mode");
 
+static bool use_irq = true;
+
+module_param(use_irq, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(use_irq, "Enable IRQ mode for the inference job, set it to 0 for polling mode.");
+
 static struct class *neutron_class;
 static dev_t devt;
 static DECLARE_BITMAP(minors, MINOR_COUNT);
@@ -84,6 +89,11 @@
 	if (power_mode == POWER_MODE_PERF)
 		ndev->suspend_delay +=  100 * MSEC_PER_SEC;
 
+	if (use_irq)
+		ndev->flags |= NEUTRON_USE_IRQ_MODE;
+	else
+		ndev->flags &= (~NEUTRON_USE_IRQ_MODE);
+
 	pm_runtime_enable(&pdev->dev);
 
 	pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(&pdev->dev, ndev->suspend_delay);
@@ -164,6 +174,10 @@
 	if (ndev->power_state == NEUTRON_POWER_ON)
 		neutron_rproc_boot(ndev, NULL);
 
+	/* Re-enable the IRQ after the system resumes from suspend */
+	if (ndev->flags & NEUTRON_USE_IRQ_MODE)
+		neutron_irq_enable(ndev);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 #endif
--- a/drivers/staging/neutron/neutron_device.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/neutron/neutron_device.c
@@ -665,6 +665,16 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+void neutron_irq_enable(struct neutron_device *ndev)
+{
+	u32 val;
+
+	/* Setup irq register */
+	val = readl(ndev->reg_base + INTENA);
+	val |= (SHUTDOWN_IRQ_ENABLE | INFERENCE_DONE_IRQ_ENABLE);
+	writel(val, ndev->reg_base + INTENA);
+}
+
 int neutron_dev_init(struct neutron_device *ndev,
 		     struct device *dev, int irq,
 		    struct class *class, dev_t devt)
